WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.900
Who owns it?

2
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.987
Every pillar already has an owner.

3
00:00:02.987 --> 00:00:06.562
What most agencies lack is an
owner for the posture itself.

4
00:00:06.562 --> 00:00:12.698
M-22-09 required each agency to designate
a zero trust strategy implementation

5
00:00:12.698 --> 00:00:16.762
lead within 30 days, and many will
give this role to that person.

6
00:00:16.762 --> 00:00:21.403
The program lead owns the definition of
the whole-agency score, what it covers

7
00:00:21.403 --> 00:00:26.262
and what it excludes, plus cross-pillar
correlation and the assessment calendar.

8
00:00:26.262 --> 00:00:29.303
The lead decides priority
but doesn't accept risk,

9
00:00:29.303 --> 00:00:34.124
and shouldn't also own the agency's
relationship with its largest cloud vendor.

10
00:00:34.124 --> 00:00:36.950
The CIO decides scope and sequence.

11
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.883
The CISO sets the evidence
standard and approves

12
00:00:39.883 --> 00:00:42.187
the tools and the accounts that run them.

13
00:00:42.187 --> 00:00:45.288
The authorizing official
accepts residual risk

14
00:00:45.288 --> 00:00:48.313
and approves each plan of
action and milestones.

15
00:00:48.313 --> 00:00:49.987
Exceptions split on time.

16
00:00:49.987 --> 00:00:53.386
An omission with an expiration
date is a CISO decision;

17
00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:58.262
one with no end date is a standing risk
acceptance for the authorizing official.

18
00:00:58.262 --> 00:01:02.810
Pillar owners decide how to fix a finding,
never that it doesn't need fixing.
